1
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:02,585
<i>You always act this way.</i>

2
00:01:02,665 --> 00:01:04,865
This is why I could never get over you.

3
00:01:04,945 --> 00:01:06,385
<i>While we're waiting for our divorce,</i>

4
00:01:06,465 --> 00:01:09,785
I can sleep with you all the time, right?

5
00:01:09,865 --> 00:01:10,945
<i>There are many more things we can do</i>

6
00:01:11,705 --> 00:01:14,945
to make it look like
we really love each other.

7
00:01:15,025 --> 00:01:16,785
Then do it all.

8
00:01:16,865 --> 00:01:18,545
What exactly are you making?

9
00:01:20,385 --> 00:01:21,265
Mom!

10
00:01:23,705 --> 00:01:24,785
Please stop. Mom will get us wrong.

11
00:01:24,865 --> 00:01:26,065
Open the door now!

12
00:01:26,145 --> 00:01:28,345
You need to back off a little, Ging.

13
00:01:28,425 --> 00:01:31,745
If I did, that would mean
I've lost to that brat.

14
00:01:53,865 --> 00:01:55,265
Yes, Mom?

15
00:01:55,345 --> 00:01:56,985
<i>I'm feeling a little dizzy.</i>

16
00:01:57,065 --> 00:02:00,465
<i>Can you take me to the hospital, Runch?</i>

17
00:02:01,305 --> 00:02:04,505
Sure. I'll be right over.

18
00:02:24,625 --> 00:02:27,825
<i>My mom's not feeling well.</i>
<i>I have to go check on her,</i>

19
00:02:27,905 --> 00:02:29,425
<i>so I might be home late.</i>

20
00:02:32,825 --> 00:02:34,625
I bet that old hag's faking it.

21
00:02:42,185 --> 00:02:45,825
-Mom? Where are you? Are you okay?
-Runch is here now.

22
00:02:49,145 --> 00:02:52,825
Forget about the hospital.
I'm feeling better now.

23
00:02:56,065 --> 00:02:59,625
Right. Runch, do you remember Maylin?

24
00:03:02,865 --> 00:03:05,585
-Maylin…?
-Maylinya.

25
00:03:05,665 --> 00:03:07,305
She is Samorn's daughter.

26
00:03:07,385 --> 00:03:09,825
You two had lots of play dates
when you were little.

27
00:03:13,305 --> 00:03:15,705
I remember her now. Maylin.

28
00:03:17,625 --> 00:03:19,385
It's been a while.

29
00:03:19,465 --> 00:03:20,865
It sure has.

30
00:03:21,545 --> 00:03:23,705
I didn't think I'd see you again so soon.

31
00:03:25,225 --> 00:03:27,865
She just got back from the US
two days ago.

32
00:03:27,945 --> 00:03:30,105
Right. Since you're already here,

33
00:03:30,185 --> 00:03:31,745
why don't you join us for dinner?

34
00:03:32,545 --> 00:03:35,785
She's got a lot to talk about with you.

35
00:03:35,865 --> 00:03:37,465
She works in the legal field too.

36
00:03:38,705 --> 00:03:41,105
Please? Pretty please?

37
00:03:42,865 --> 00:03:44,065
Sure, Mom.

38
00:03:52,225 --> 00:03:54,385
-Help yourself, honey.
-Thank you.

39
00:03:56,985 --> 00:04:01,225
She's starting a new job next week,
so she wants your advice.

40
00:04:03,105 --> 00:04:04,545
Sure thing, Maylin.

41
00:04:05,305 --> 00:04:08,865
It takes great attention to detail
to work in the legal field.

42
00:04:09,385 --> 00:04:10,945
And more importantly,

43
00:04:11,025 --> 00:04:13,145
you must treat your clients as humans,

44
00:04:13,225 --> 00:04:14,705
not cases.

45
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:18,384
Sometimes, the things they don't say

46
00:04:18,465 --> 00:04:21,105
matter more than what they do say.

47
00:04:27,945 --> 00:04:29,865
Well said, Runch.

48
00:04:29,945 --> 00:04:32,305
I'm glad to see you again.

49
00:04:32,385 --> 00:04:35,825
If you don't mind,
can I add you so we can text?

50
00:04:37,185 --> 00:04:38,065
Of course.

51
00:04:39,185 --> 00:04:40,145
Here you go.

52
00:04:46,945 --> 00:04:47,785
Done.

53
00:04:47,865 --> 00:04:49,185
Thank you.

54
00:04:55,745 --> 00:04:57,025
Dig in, Runch.

55
00:04:57,105 --> 00:04:58,385
Sure.

56
00:05:10,065 --> 00:05:11,505
Neen.

57
00:05:45,025 --> 00:05:49,185
Neen, can you open the door for me?
I'm home.

58
00:05:49,905 --> 00:05:51,065
What is it?

59
00:05:53,465 --> 00:05:55,545
I see you've bought me dinner.

60
00:06:01,345 --> 00:06:04,225
What? Who bought you dinner? I didn't.

61
00:06:05,385 --> 00:06:07,705
But they're all my favorite dishes.

62
00:06:08,985 --> 00:06:11,145
You were waiting
to have dinner with me, right?

63
00:06:11,225 --> 00:06:14,345
No, I wasn't. Why would I?
I have no reason to.

64
00:06:22,905 --> 00:06:23,785
Here.

65
00:06:25,505 --> 00:06:27,425
Here's your appetizer.

66
00:06:29,905 --> 00:06:30,985
I'm not hungry.

67
00:06:36,705 --> 00:06:41,705
Your stomach just protested, though.

68
00:06:50,945 --> 00:06:52,345
I told you I'm not hungry.

69
00:06:53,425 --> 00:06:56,825
Don't be upset and hangry now.

70
00:06:57,585 --> 00:06:59,265
Let's go downstairs and eat.

71
00:07:00,665 --> 00:07:02,705
Either come downstairs,

72
00:07:03,225 --> 00:07:04,825
or I'll carry you.

73
00:07:05,585 --> 00:07:08,025
Your choice.

74
00:07:29,225 --> 00:07:31,385
Here we go.

75
00:07:32,465 --> 00:07:35,425
-Fried rice. Nice and hot.
-Thank you.

76
00:07:36,905 --> 00:07:38,305
-Go ahead.
-May I?

77
00:07:39,025 --> 00:07:40,545
Dig in.

78
00:07:41,865 --> 00:07:43,505
You must be hungry.

79
00:07:51,225 --> 00:07:52,945
So how's your mother?

80
00:07:53,705 --> 00:07:55,585
She has high blood pressure.

81
00:07:55,665 --> 00:07:57,345
High blood pressure?

82
00:07:57,985 --> 00:08:00,465
She called you just for that?

83
00:08:01,465 --> 00:08:04,185
Well, at first,
I was going to take her to the hospital.

84
00:08:06,705 --> 00:08:09,825
That means you didn't.

85
00:08:10,465 --> 00:08:11,745
Why not?

86
00:08:12,945 --> 00:08:15,385
She's feeling better now,
so I didn't need to.

87
00:08:16,025 --> 00:08:17,505
I knew it.

88
00:08:17,585 --> 00:08:19,265
She was faking it.

89
00:08:19,345 --> 00:08:21,265
She just wanted you to go see her.

90
00:08:21,985 --> 00:08:24,545
You always fall for her tricks.

91
00:08:26,665 --> 00:08:28,305
She's my mom.

92
00:08:28,385 --> 00:08:33,024
Either way, I had to go check on her
so I could rest easy.

93
00:08:34,745 --> 00:08:36,144
Sure.

94
00:08:36,225 --> 00:08:38,144
What a wonderful daughter you are.

95
00:08:40,264 --> 00:08:41,585
Let's eat.

96
00:08:55,185 --> 00:08:59,265
Aren't you going to read that text?

97
00:08:59,865 --> 00:09:01,345
No.

98
00:09:01,425 --> 00:09:04,345
Because I'm having dinner
with you right now.

99
00:09:04,425 --> 00:09:06,425
I don't care about anything else.

100
00:09:07,105 --> 00:09:08,025
Okay.

101
00:09:15,025 --> 00:09:16,585
Okay, Mom.

102
00:09:17,585 --> 00:09:19,985
Tomorrow's my day off,
so I'll come right over.

103
00:09:20,865 --> 00:09:23,745
Sure. Talk to you later. Okay.

104
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:27,825
Where are you going, Neen?

105
00:09:30,185 --> 00:09:32,105
My mom said my grandparents miss me.

106
00:09:32,185 --> 00:09:34,705
She told me to visit them
whenever I'm free,

107
00:09:34,785 --> 00:09:36,665
so I'm thinking I'll go tomorrow.

108
00:09:36,745 --> 00:09:41,025
Perfect. I've missed them.
Can I come with?

109
00:09:41,545 --> 00:09:43,105
Who invited you?

110
00:09:43,985 --> 00:09:45,665
I'm going alone.

111
00:09:45,745 --> 00:09:48,465
I don't think that's a good idea.

112
00:09:48,545 --> 00:09:51,905
What if they ask about me?

113
00:09:51,985 --> 00:09:53,705
What will you tell them?

114
00:09:54,625 --> 00:09:56,985
That we're getting divorced?

115
00:09:58,025 --> 00:10:01,105
They'd be crushed.

116
00:10:02,225 --> 00:10:03,625
Let's go together.

117
00:10:03,705 --> 00:10:07,065
-So it's settled. I'm off to work now.
-No, Runch.

118
00:10:07,145 --> 00:10:08,305
Runch!

119
00:10:26,465 --> 00:10:27,465
What are you doing?

120
00:10:30,505 --> 00:10:32,425
I'm doing the packing for you.

121
00:10:33,545 --> 00:10:37,665
Mind your own business, will you?
It's my stuff. I can do it myself.

122
00:10:38,665 --> 00:10:42,065
I just wanted you
to feel as relaxed as you can.

123
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:47,945
Thank you. But please don't do it again.

124
00:10:49,305 --> 00:10:51,345
I'll still do it for you

125
00:10:52,145 --> 00:10:56,305
because I know you always
forget something when you pack.

126
00:10:56,385 --> 00:10:59,265
That's not true. I know how to pack.

127
00:11:01,465 --> 00:11:02,825
But…

128
00:11:03,425 --> 00:11:06,585
I do forget sunscreen sometimes.

129
00:11:07,345 --> 00:11:10,865
That's exactly why I had to pack for you.

130
00:11:18,665 --> 00:11:20,025
How nice.

131
00:11:21,625 --> 00:11:22,705
What was that?

132
00:11:24,625 --> 00:11:25,785
Nothing.

133
00:11:25,865 --> 00:11:27,425
Oh?

134
00:11:27,505 --> 00:11:30,065
Go pack for yourself. I'm going to shower.

135
00:11:32,425 --> 00:11:34,305
What if

136
00:11:34,385 --> 00:11:36,625
I want to shower with you?

137
00:11:37,225 --> 00:11:39,345
No. Get out already.

138
00:11:40,945 --> 00:11:43,785
-Go.
-I'm not done yet.

139
00:11:46,185 --> 00:11:48,345
I can pack for myself. Just go shower.

140
00:11:48,425 --> 00:11:50,825
Are you sure you can?

141
00:12:18,585 --> 00:12:20,945
Are you free to talk, Maylin?

142
00:12:21,625 --> 00:12:24,585
I wanted to invite you over for lunch

143
00:12:24,665 --> 00:12:26,065
since it's the weekend.

144
00:12:26,145 --> 00:12:28,385
Runch will be here too.

145
00:12:28,465 --> 00:12:30,025
You're coming, right?

146
00:12:30,105 --> 00:12:33,505
Once the food's been delivered,
I'll call you right away.

147
00:12:33,585 --> 00:12:34,705
Thanks.

148
00:12:36,065 --> 00:12:37,625
Who's this Maylin?

149
00:12:37,705 --> 00:12:38,985
Oh.

150
00:12:39,065 --> 00:12:41,745
It's Samorn's daughter. Remember her?

151
00:12:41,825 --> 00:12:43,985
We used to see her when she was little.

152
00:12:45,105 --> 00:12:46,865
Ah. I remember now.

153
00:12:46,945 --> 00:12:49,585
She's the cute little girl
who always followed Runch around.

154
00:12:49,665 --> 00:12:51,705
-Yeah.
-Isn't she studying abroad?

155
00:12:52,305 --> 00:12:55,705
She was, but she just got back recently.

156
00:12:55,785 --> 00:12:57,065
She came to see me yesterday

157
00:12:57,145 --> 00:12:59,265
and gave me a souvenir
as soon as she got back.

158
00:12:59,345 --> 00:13:00,865
How sweet of her.

159
00:13:01,545 --> 00:13:05,185
She has such a pretty face and body.
And she's well-mannered too.

160
00:13:07,425 --> 00:13:08,985
What a shame.

161
00:13:09,785 --> 00:13:10,985
What do you mean?

162
00:13:12,705 --> 00:13:15,225
It's a shame
she and Runch didn't meet sooner.

163
00:13:15,305 --> 00:13:17,745
I would've asked her
to marry our daughter.

164
00:13:17,825 --> 00:13:19,265
How can you think that?

165
00:13:19,345 --> 00:13:21,905
Why can't I? It's just a thought.

166
00:13:21,985 --> 00:13:23,265
Well, I sure hope so.

167
00:13:24,145 --> 00:13:26,025
Don't do anything immoral.

168
00:13:26,865 --> 00:13:28,025
What do you mean?

169
00:13:28,105 --> 00:13:31,305
Don't break up a couple. I'm warning you.

170
00:13:32,865 --> 00:13:35,145
You know me too well.
But I'm not afraid of sinning.

171
00:13:35,985 --> 00:13:37,745
I'd better call Runch.

172
00:13:57,185 --> 00:14:00,665
MOM

173
00:14:03,585 --> 00:14:06,505
Answer it, or your mom
will just keep calling all day.

174
00:14:10,265 --> 00:14:11,585
-Yes, Mom?
<i>-Runch,</i>

175
00:14:12,185 --> 00:14:13,865
please join me for lunch today.

176
00:14:14,665 --> 00:14:16,705
I can't today.

177
00:14:16,785 --> 00:14:20,785
What? Where are you going?
Are you busy all day or something?

178
00:14:21,785 --> 00:14:24,825
Can't you eat with your mom
for just a couple hours?

179
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:27,825
I really can't today, Mom.

180
00:14:28,665 --> 00:14:30,425
<i>But I invited Maylin over.</i>

181
00:14:31,425 --> 00:14:33,025
<i>She wants to see you.</i>

182
00:14:35,945 --> 00:14:38,185
I really can't, Mom.

183
00:14:38,265 --> 00:14:42,585
Neen and I are on our way to visit
her grandparents at their country house.

184
00:14:43,345 --> 00:14:47,025
Why didn't you call and tell me first?
I already invited Maylin over.

185
00:14:47,105 --> 00:14:49,705
<i>She'll be so sad that you're not here.</i>

186
00:14:52,865 --> 00:14:56,225
How far away are you?
Can't you drive back now?

187
00:14:57,025 --> 00:14:58,825
<i>Join us for lunch and then go.</i>

188
00:14:58,905 --> 00:15:01,425
You expect her to drive back and forth?

189
00:15:01,505 --> 00:15:05,585
We're already over halfway there.
We don't want to bother going back now.

190
00:15:05,665 --> 00:15:07,305
Wait. You're on speaker?

191
00:15:07,385 --> 00:15:10,745
Yes, Mom. I'm driving.

192
00:15:11,345 --> 00:15:13,185
We can't make it today, Mom.

193
00:15:13,265 --> 00:15:17,385
Please tell that Maylin girl of yours
that if she's so sad,

194
00:15:17,465 --> 00:15:19,705
you'll buy her a lollipop.

195
00:15:19,785 --> 00:15:22,825
Talk to you later.
Runch needs to focus on the road.

196
00:15:28,985 --> 00:15:32,505
You brat. Did you just hang up on me?

197
00:15:45,865 --> 00:15:49,905
Neen, why are you mad at me?

198
00:15:49,985 --> 00:15:51,385
I'm not.

199
00:15:51,465 --> 00:15:54,785
You're lying. I can tell you're mad.

200
00:15:54,865 --> 00:15:57,465
I can explain about Maylin.

201
00:15:59,465 --> 00:16:01,905
So you knew. Why'd you ask then?

202
00:16:03,065 --> 00:16:04,505
You're obviously

203
00:16:05,385 --> 00:16:06,905
-feeling jealous.
-I'm not.

204
00:16:08,065 --> 00:16:10,665
Why would I get jealous?
We're getting divorced anyway.

205
00:16:11,265 --> 00:16:14,225
Maylin is the daughter
of one of my mom's close friends.

206
00:16:14,305 --> 00:16:16,505
We used to play together
when we were little.

207
00:16:16,585 --> 00:16:18,945
That's all. There's nothing more.

208
00:16:20,465 --> 00:16:23,265
Your mom seems to hope for more

209
00:16:23,345 --> 00:16:24,985
since she arranged for you to meet.

210
00:16:27,585 --> 00:16:29,345
Neen.

211
00:16:34,025 --> 00:16:37,185
Don't get upset. Please?

212
00:16:38,985 --> 00:16:41,785
When your grandparents see your face,

213
00:16:41,865 --> 00:16:44,025
they'll be able to tell you're upset.

214
00:16:44,905 --> 00:16:46,945
That'll only make them worried.

215
00:16:48,465 --> 00:16:50,825
They want to see us happy together.

216
00:16:53,225 --> 00:16:54,905
Let's hold hands and head inside.

217
00:17:11,265 --> 00:17:13,345
Grandpa. Grandma.

218
00:17:13,865 --> 00:17:16,665
What brings you here?

219
00:17:16,745 --> 00:17:19,464
I came because
I've missed you both, of course.

220
00:17:19,545 --> 00:17:20,785
Aw,

221
00:17:20,865 --> 00:17:24,905
you're quite the sweet-talker, aren't you?
I've missed you too.

222
00:17:24,985 --> 00:17:27,464
-Me too.
-Let me give her a hug too.

223
00:17:27,545 --> 00:17:30,345
-So impatient, this guy.
-Aw.

224
00:17:34,905 --> 00:17:36,665
You're way too small.

225
00:17:36,745 --> 00:17:38,905
Are you sure you've been eating enough?

226
00:17:38,985 --> 00:17:41,545
Or does Runch want you
to have a model-type body?

227
00:17:42,825 --> 00:17:45,545
I didn't ask her to eat less

228
00:17:45,625 --> 00:17:47,705
so she could have a model-type body.

229
00:17:48,785 --> 00:17:50,465
I've been eating plenty.

230
00:17:50,545 --> 00:17:52,825
Don't worry, Grandpa.
I'm healthy and well.

231
00:17:54,745 --> 00:17:55,625
Runch.

232
00:17:56,185 --> 00:17:58,105
It's been a while.

233
00:17:58,745 --> 00:18:00,585
You're even prettier than I remember.

234
00:18:00,665 --> 00:18:01,825
Thank you.

235
00:18:03,785 --> 00:18:04,945
What about me?

236
00:18:07,425 --> 00:18:10,865
Of course you're the prettiest for me.

237
00:18:14,185 --> 00:18:16,785
How have you both been?
Are you doing alright?

238
00:18:16,865 --> 00:18:18,985
-Yes.
-We've been great.

239
00:18:28,905 --> 00:18:31,185
Grandma asked you what you want for lunch.

240
00:18:32,065 --> 00:18:33,345
Anything is fine.

241
00:18:34,065 --> 00:18:35,305
I'll tell her that.

242
00:18:37,425 --> 00:18:39,825
Wanna go for a walk? It's nice out today.

243
00:18:43,585 --> 00:18:44,785
Sure.

244
00:18:44,865 --> 00:18:46,905
It's been a while
since we last went for a walk.

245
00:18:47,825 --> 00:18:51,345
Before, we used to do it so often.

246
00:18:53,945 --> 00:18:55,065
Okay.

247
00:18:55,705 --> 00:18:58,825
Let's go for a post-meal walk
for our digestion.

248
00:19:08,585 --> 00:19:11,945
You say it's for digestion. But really,

249
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:14,465
you just want to spend time with me,
don't you?

250
00:19:14,985 --> 00:19:16,745
I know you do.

251
00:19:27,305 --> 00:19:29,905
Let's eat and then
go for a post-meal walk.

252
00:19:31,265 --> 00:19:32,425
Come on.

253
00:19:39,985 --> 00:19:42,745
Do you want to live like my grandparents?

254
00:19:43,905 --> 00:19:47,185
I bet you won't like having to stay here.

255
00:19:48,865 --> 00:19:51,945
I was asking you.
Do you like living that way?

256
00:19:52,985 --> 00:19:55,025
I just like being with you.

257
00:19:58,225 --> 00:19:59,505
You're so full of it.

258
00:20:18,345 --> 00:20:19,785
Flowers for you.

259
00:20:22,305 --> 00:20:25,745
Are you always this cheap
when giving flowers to a girl, gorgeous?

260
00:20:28,665 --> 00:20:32,265
I'm not like you,
Ms. Peeracha Pacharathakul.

261
00:20:32,345 --> 00:20:35,145
You bought an expensive bouquet
of flowers just to congratulate

262
00:20:35,225 --> 00:20:38,145
an Employee of the Year.

263
00:20:38,985 --> 00:20:40,785
You liked it though, didn't you?

264
00:20:43,345 --> 00:20:44,905
Actually…

265
00:20:45,985 --> 00:20:47,865
it did give me mixed emotions.

266
00:21:03,025 --> 00:21:05,065
Congratulations on winning
Employee of the Year.

267
00:21:05,145 --> 00:21:06,185
And the promotion too.

268
00:21:10,705 --> 00:21:14,145
Thank you. How'd you know about this?

269
00:21:15,025 --> 00:21:18,865
Well, my last name is Pacharathakul.

270
00:21:20,265 --> 00:21:21,785
Pacharathakul?

271
00:21:22,625 --> 00:21:26,465
You have the same last name
as Mr. Apichet, my boss.

272
00:21:27,985 --> 00:21:28,905
Yes.

273
00:21:30,545 --> 00:21:32,865
He's my uncle.

274
00:21:37,225 --> 00:21:39,025
It's a beautiful family name, right?

275
00:21:39,105 --> 00:21:40,545
Want to adopt it?

276
00:21:47,425 --> 00:21:49,985
The award and the promotion I got,

277
00:21:51,145 --> 00:21:53,305
you had nothing to do with it, right?

278
00:21:54,225 --> 00:21:57,065
We're not even a couple yet.
Why would I do that?

279
00:21:57,145 --> 00:22:00,785
So if we were a couple, you'd do it?

280
00:22:01,865 --> 00:22:03,145
No.

281
00:22:04,505 --> 00:22:06,785
If you don't believe me, let's become one.

282
00:22:08,305 --> 00:22:09,265
I'm sorry?

283
00:22:11,945 --> 00:22:13,705
I'm asking you to be my girlfriend.

284
00:22:13,785 --> 00:22:15,305
Huh?

285
00:22:16,785 --> 00:22:17,945
Will you be my girlfriend?

286
00:22:19,785 --> 00:22:21,545
I'm sorry, what? Give me a second.

287
00:22:24,865 --> 00:22:26,105
Are you worried?

288
00:22:26,745 --> 00:22:28,505
Well, aren't you?

289
00:22:28,585 --> 00:22:30,785
We've been
getting along great, haven't we?

290
00:22:31,305 --> 00:22:34,265
Well… Yes, we have.

291
00:22:36,105 --> 00:22:39,265
That means we can date, no?

292
00:22:42,825 --> 00:22:45,825
Fine, fine.
I'll give you some time to think.

293
00:22:51,665 --> 00:22:52,945
I'm done thinking.

294
00:22:54,145 --> 00:22:55,225
The answer is yes.

295
00:22:59,945 --> 00:23:00,785
‎Wait.

296
00:23:01,425 --> 00:23:02,945
Enough.

297
00:23:03,025 --> 00:23:06,025
Someone will see us.

298
00:23:08,025 --> 00:23:09,265
Fine.

299
00:23:09,945 --> 00:23:11,905
We can take a rain check.

300
00:23:12,425 --> 00:23:15,265
Next time, I won't hold back.

301
00:23:32,305 --> 00:23:33,825
So you remember?

302
00:23:35,025 --> 00:23:37,265
If it has to do with you,

303
00:23:38,265 --> 00:23:39,785
I'll always remember.

304
00:23:47,385 --> 00:23:48,705
Let's head inside.

305
00:23:49,385 --> 00:23:51,385
My grandparents are waiting
to have lunch with us.

306
00:23:51,465 --> 00:23:52,625
Let's go.

307
00:23:54,865 --> 00:23:56,225
Did I make you blush?

308
00:23:57,945 --> 00:23:59,425
What? Why would I be blushing?

309
00:23:59,505 --> 00:24:00,465
Your face is all red.

310
00:24:00,545 --> 00:24:02,945
It's hot. I'm feeling hot.

311
00:24:04,585 --> 00:24:05,905
Stay here if you want.

312
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:13,345
What did you do to make
your relationship last to this day?

313
00:24:14,585 --> 00:24:17,705
I don't know how it's done either.

314
00:24:17,785 --> 00:24:22,305
There's no specific method
that can be applied to every couple.

315
00:24:22,945 --> 00:24:26,105
All I can say is,
be patient with each other.

316
00:24:26,745 --> 00:24:27,825
Being patient

317
00:24:27,905 --> 00:24:29,905
may sound like a simple task,

318
00:24:29,985 --> 00:24:33,505
but for some people, it can be difficult.

319
00:24:33,585 --> 00:24:35,145
I agree.

320
00:24:35,225 --> 00:24:37,185
It's complicated

321
00:24:37,985 --> 00:24:40,585
when it comes to
maintaining a relationship.

322
00:24:40,665 --> 00:24:43,825
Your grandma and I
are still together to this day

323
00:24:44,745 --> 00:24:47,465
only because we've been
through so much together.

324
00:24:48,105 --> 00:24:49,665
We've fought.

325
00:24:51,145 --> 00:24:52,945
We've had disagreements.

326
00:24:53,025 --> 00:24:57,745
We've cried more times than we can count.

327
00:24:59,865 --> 00:25:03,465
Your wedding last year

328
00:25:04,065 --> 00:25:06,025
was just the beginning.

329
00:25:06,105 --> 00:25:07,505
Like I said,

330
00:25:09,065 --> 00:25:11,505
be patient with each other.

331
00:25:11,585 --> 00:25:15,465
Being direct but in a patient way

332
00:25:15,545 --> 00:25:19,065
can make big problems small.

333
00:25:19,145 --> 00:25:23,145
Staying patient
is a way to pull yourself together.

334
00:25:23,225 --> 00:25:27,345
Think before you speak or act.

335
00:25:27,425 --> 00:25:29,505
Don't act on your emotions.

336
00:25:29,585 --> 00:25:32,345
It'll only make matters worse.

337
00:25:32,425 --> 00:25:34,905
So, which of you

338
00:25:35,465 --> 00:25:36,665
is more patient?

339
00:25:39,025 --> 00:25:41,225
Probably him.

340
00:25:41,305 --> 00:25:42,905
Because I've been

341
00:25:42,985 --> 00:25:45,505
as intense as fire since I was young.

342
00:25:48,985 --> 00:25:52,385
What makes you more patient then?

343
00:25:53,665 --> 00:25:57,025
It's probably his handsome face.

344
00:25:57,105 --> 00:25:59,105
Same here.

345
00:25:59,185 --> 00:26:01,425
I guess I took after you, Grandma,

346
00:26:02,425 --> 00:26:05,185
because every time I see her pretty face,

347
00:26:05,265 --> 00:26:07,745
I always go soft on her.

348
00:26:08,665 --> 00:26:11,105
Seeing you both like this makes me happy.

349
00:26:11,985 --> 00:26:13,705
I hope you'll love each other

350
00:26:13,785 --> 00:26:15,985
and stay together until you die.

351
00:26:29,265 --> 00:26:31,545
You just need to
move those roses to a pot.

352
00:26:31,625 --> 00:26:33,745
-Can you do that?
-Sure.

353
00:26:34,505 --> 00:26:37,385
I used to buy trees and plant them myself.

354
00:26:37,465 --> 00:26:39,145
But now I have a job,
so I don't have time.

355
00:26:39,225 --> 00:26:41,025
Perfect, then.

356
00:26:41,105 --> 00:26:43,345
I'm counting on you.

357
00:26:43,425 --> 00:26:44,705
-Sure, Grandma.
-Okay.

358
00:26:57,505 --> 00:27:00,185
I never knew you could garden.

359
00:27:01,385 --> 00:27:03,145
In my college years,

360
00:27:03,225 --> 00:27:05,425
I used to love shopping
at the plant market

361
00:27:05,505 --> 00:27:07,265
to buy plants and plant them myself.

362
00:27:07,345 --> 00:27:09,825
But now I have a job,
so I don't have time.

363
00:27:09,905 --> 00:27:10,865
Come here.

364
00:27:16,185 --> 00:27:17,265
Okay.

365
00:27:24,545 --> 00:27:26,065
Do you remember?

366
00:27:26,145 --> 00:27:29,345
White roses are my favorite.

367
00:27:29,425 --> 00:27:30,785
Of course I do.

368
00:27:32,425 --> 00:27:34,345
Do you remember why?

369
00:27:36,625 --> 00:27:38,265
I don't know.

370
00:27:38,345 --> 00:27:39,465
Because they're pretty?

371
00:27:40,505 --> 00:27:42,985
White roses symbolize

372
00:27:43,065 --> 00:27:46,465
a love that is innocent and beautiful

373
00:27:47,185 --> 00:27:50,025
as well as eternal love
and new beginnings.

374
00:27:52,825 --> 00:27:54,545
How cheesy.

375
00:27:55,665 --> 00:27:56,945
Eternal love?

376
00:27:57,745 --> 00:27:59,425
That doesn't exist.

377
00:28:08,225 --> 00:28:09,425
Why are you laughing?

378
00:28:10,505 --> 00:28:13,825
No, I'm not laughing. I'm not.

379
00:28:13,905 --> 00:28:15,145
Wha…

380
00:28:15,225 --> 00:28:16,705
What?

381
00:28:21,905 --> 00:28:23,545
Is there something on my face?

382
00:28:25,385 --> 00:28:27,065
I'll get it for you.

383
00:28:29,745 --> 00:28:32,785
How cute.

384
00:28:32,865 --> 00:28:35,265
You're cute even when your face is dirty.

385
00:28:37,585 --> 00:28:39,265
There. All better.

386
00:28:41,145 --> 00:28:43,345
Get it off completely. Is it all gone?

387
00:28:43,425 --> 00:28:46,905
I'll wash your face after this.

388
00:28:46,985 --> 00:28:48,665
It's all gone now.

389
00:29:24,825 --> 00:29:26,345
Grandpa! Grandma!

390
00:29:27,825 --> 00:29:29,945
Runch and I are done planting the roses.

391
00:29:30,025 --> 00:29:32,265
Can I help you with anything else?

392
00:29:43,345 --> 00:29:44,745
It's huge.

393
00:29:45,465 --> 00:29:46,985
How are we going to wash it?

394
00:29:49,465 --> 00:29:50,985
I know a way.

395
00:29:59,745 --> 00:30:01,185
Hmm?

396
00:30:01,265 --> 00:30:04,665
I didn't know you can wash it this way.
It's pretty fun.

397
00:30:23,025 --> 00:30:24,625
You can let go now.

398
00:30:24,705 --> 00:30:27,585
If I do that, you'll fall.

399
00:30:29,385 --> 00:30:31,825
Let's just keep hugging.
It warms my heart.

400
00:30:34,585 --> 00:30:35,545
Okay.

401
00:30:49,465 --> 00:30:50,345
Oh!

402
00:30:50,425 --> 00:30:52,985
Quick. Take a photo.

403
00:30:57,505 --> 00:30:59,225
Send it. Send it.

404
00:31:00,025 --> 00:31:00,985
HOW'S EVERYTHING, MOM?

405
00:31:01,065 --> 00:31:02,505
There we go.

406
00:31:03,385 --> 00:31:04,865
<i>Did it send, Kae?</i>

407
00:31:04,945 --> 00:31:08,425
We saw it, Mom.
I hope your plan will succeed.

408
00:31:08,505 --> 00:31:10,465
Of course it will.

409
00:31:10,545 --> 00:31:13,465
I'll try my best to make them

410
00:31:13,545 --> 00:31:16,265
change their mind about the divorce.

411
00:31:16,345 --> 00:31:18,505
<i>Surely, this visit</i>

412
00:31:18,585 --> 00:31:20,265
will make them feel something.

413
00:31:21,305 --> 00:31:22,705
We're counting on you, Mom.

414
00:31:22,785 --> 00:31:26,625
We really don't want Neen and Runch
to get divorced.

415
00:31:26,705 --> 00:31:30,825
Yeah, that's right.
Just thinking about it breaks my heart.

416
00:31:30,905 --> 00:31:33,865
I'd understand if they got divorced
because of a conflict.

417
00:31:33,945 --> 00:31:36,865
But they're doing it because of
someone else. I can't accept it.

418
00:31:36,945 --> 00:31:39,145
We don't know what to do either.

419
00:31:39,225 --> 00:31:42,945
When she told us they'd get divorced,
all we could do was listen.

420
00:31:43,025 --> 00:31:44,745
But we definitely don't want that.

421
00:31:45,625 --> 00:31:47,225
But judging from the photo,

422
00:31:47,305 --> 00:31:49,745
if we let them stay there
for two more weeks,

423
00:31:49,825 --> 00:31:52,345
no one will need to push them.
They'll make up on their own.

424
00:31:57,425 --> 00:31:59,145
You can count on me.

425
00:31:59,985 --> 00:32:02,065
Don't you even worry.

426
00:32:23,825 --> 00:32:26,785
I'm sorry. Runch couldn't make it.

427
00:32:26,865 --> 00:32:28,985
She has some urgent work to do.

428
00:32:30,985 --> 00:32:34,545
No worries, Aunt Ging. I understand.

429
00:32:34,625 --> 00:32:37,745
Lawyers have little time to rest.

430
00:32:39,265 --> 00:32:42,625
You're so sweet for understanding Runch.

431
00:32:43,945 --> 00:32:46,465
Well, I've always idolized her
since I was little.

432
00:32:47,065 --> 00:32:50,025
She's just so cool,
no matter what she does.

433
00:32:50,105 --> 00:32:53,385
I even got a law degree because of her.

434
00:32:54,425 --> 00:32:55,985
Runch used to tell me

435
00:32:56,065 --> 00:32:58,305
she wanted to be a lawyer
when she grew up,

436
00:32:58,385 --> 00:32:59,745
and she really did.

437
00:33:01,425 --> 00:33:03,625
That's why I wanted to be like her.

438
00:33:04,345 --> 00:33:06,545
You seem to really like her.

439
00:33:07,945 --> 00:33:09,705
Yes, I do.

440
00:33:12,785 --> 00:33:14,505
Maylin.

441
00:33:14,585 --> 00:33:16,425
Can I ask you something?

442
00:33:17,105 --> 00:33:17,945
Sure.

443
00:33:18,025 --> 00:33:20,025
You have a crush on her, right?

444
00:33:23,105 --> 00:33:24,585
Aunt Ging!

445
00:33:27,785 --> 00:33:29,185
You can be honest with me.

446
00:33:29,265 --> 00:33:32,425
These days, it's normal
for women to like women.

447
00:33:32,505 --> 00:33:33,985
I understand.

448
00:33:38,665 --> 00:33:39,865
Yes.

449
00:33:40,665 --> 00:33:42,385
I have a crush on her.

450
00:33:43,305 --> 00:33:45,065
For a while now too.

451
00:33:50,225 --> 00:33:51,345
Help yourself, honey.

452
00:33:51,425 --> 00:33:52,625
Thank you.

453
00:34:02,345 --> 00:34:03,185
Runch.

454
00:34:03,265 --> 00:34:04,265
Come here for a second.

455
00:34:04,345 --> 00:34:06,345
Yes?

456
00:34:06,425 --> 00:34:07,665
Come here.

457
00:34:10,025 --> 00:34:11,505
Neen's taking a shower, right?

458
00:34:11,585 --> 00:34:14,705
Yes, she just got in the bathroom.
Is something wrong?

459
00:34:14,784 --> 00:34:16,824
We have something important to tell you.

460
00:34:16,905 --> 00:34:18,665
Something important?

461
00:34:19,585 --> 00:34:22,784
Her birthday
is coming up in a few days.

462
00:34:23,545 --> 00:34:25,264
Yes, I know that.

463
00:34:26,105 --> 00:34:30,304
We wanted to plan
a surprise for her in advance

464
00:34:30,385 --> 00:34:31,705
here, at our country house.

465
00:34:32,865 --> 00:34:33,905
That way,

466
00:34:33,985 --> 00:34:36,505
we can give her mind and heart a rest.

467
00:34:36,585 --> 00:34:39,225
And she'll get to be happy for real.

468
00:34:40,145 --> 00:34:41,425
It's been a while

469
00:34:41,505 --> 00:34:46,425
since her grandma and I
heard her laugh like she used to.

470
00:34:47,985 --> 00:34:50,665
Please help me out, Runch.

471
00:34:51,705 --> 00:34:55,465
You're the only one
who knows her the best.

472
00:34:58,425 --> 00:35:00,825
Sure, Grandpa, Grandma.

473
00:35:00,905 --> 00:35:02,985
I'll handle everything for you.

474
00:35:04,585 --> 00:35:07,105
Neen is such a lucky girl

475
00:35:07,185 --> 00:35:09,745
to have someone
who loves her so sincerely.

476
00:35:12,545 --> 00:35:14,145
Let's plan it together.

477
00:35:14,745 --> 00:35:16,865
And keep it a secret from her.

478
00:35:17,465 --> 00:35:18,425
Sure.

479
00:35:25,505 --> 00:35:27,465
-This one's really good.
-Thanks.

480
00:35:28,065 --> 00:35:29,305
Have this too.

481
00:35:31,585 --> 00:35:32,465
Neen.

482
00:35:32,545 --> 00:35:35,785
Your grandma and I
are going to an event at the temple.

483
00:35:36,665 --> 00:35:39,945
Can you give us a ride?

484
00:35:41,505 --> 00:35:43,705
Of course. I'll give you a ride.

485
00:35:44,545 --> 00:35:47,465
Please watch over our house, Runch.

486
00:35:48,065 --> 00:35:49,625
You don't have to do much.

487
00:35:49,705 --> 00:35:51,905
Putting away the plates and bowls
would be enough.

488
00:35:51,985 --> 00:35:53,745
Sure, Grandma.

489
00:35:53,825 --> 00:35:56,065
I'll make sure everything's nice and neat.

490
00:35:56,865 --> 00:35:59,545
Perfect. Shall we go
after we're done eating?

491
00:35:59,625 --> 00:36:00,665
-Sure.
-Okay?

492
00:36:02,825 --> 00:36:03,985
Dig in.

493
00:37:02,505 --> 00:37:03,785
Runch.

494
00:37:07,305 --> 00:37:08,625
Runch?

495
00:37:13,265 --> 00:37:14,745
Runch, where are you?

496
00:37:40,945 --> 00:37:42,185
Runch?

497
00:37:44,265 --> 00:37:45,265
Runch.

498
00:37:50,745 --> 00:37:51,985
Runch.

499
00:38:43,385 --> 00:38:44,545
Runch.

500
00:38:53,345 --> 00:38:54,985
What's this about?

501
00:39:00,545 --> 00:39:02,505
In advance of your birthday, Neen.

502
00:39:04,065 --> 00:39:06,105
Make a wish and blow out the candles.

503
00:39:36,145 --> 00:39:40,185
Tonight, your grandparents
won't be coming home.

504
00:39:41,065 --> 00:39:43,385
They're staying at a friend's house.

505
00:39:44,425 --> 00:39:48,065
Yeah. That's what they told me too.

506
00:39:49,265 --> 00:39:51,385
So that means

507
00:39:52,625 --> 00:39:56,745
there will be just the two of us tonight.

508
00:39:57,345 --> 00:39:58,385
Yeah.

509
00:40:00,065 --> 00:40:01,265
So,

510
00:40:02,745 --> 00:40:04,705
what are we doing tonight?

511
00:40:19,705 --> 00:40:21,065
How pretty.

512
00:40:22,065 --> 00:40:24,705
You know,
I've never stargazed here before.

513
00:40:26,745 --> 00:40:28,145
I know.

514
00:40:28,905 --> 00:40:31,905
That's why I wanted
to look at the stars with you tonight.

515
00:40:38,105 --> 00:40:39,385
Did you know?

516
00:40:39,945 --> 00:40:42,865
I used to love stargazing
when I was little.

517
00:40:43,785 --> 00:40:46,985
But now that I'm grown,
I hardly ever look up at the sky.

518
00:40:51,745 --> 00:40:52,665
Whoa!

519
00:40:53,345 --> 00:40:54,505
Runch,

520
00:40:55,265 --> 00:40:56,545
did you see that shooting star?

521
00:41:00,545 --> 00:41:01,785
An actual shooting star--

522
00:42:20,865 --> 00:42:22,625
That's a pretty sunset, isn't it?

523
00:42:22,705 --> 00:42:23,705
3 YEARS AGO

524
00:42:23,785 --> 00:42:26,625
It's nothing compared to you.

525
00:42:29,265 --> 00:42:30,905
You're quite the sweet-talker.

526
00:42:32,225 --> 00:42:33,505
Have you tasted my lips?

527
00:42:33,585 --> 00:42:35,385
How do you know they're sweet?

528
00:42:35,985 --> 00:42:37,225
No, I haven't.

529
00:42:39,425 --> 00:42:40,625
But now I kind of want to.

530
00:42:41,505 --> 00:42:43,345
I wonder if they really are sweet.

531
00:42:46,145 --> 00:42:48,385
Today's our first day as a couple.

532
00:42:49,625 --> 00:42:52,265
May I kiss you?

533
00:43:38,305 --> 00:43:42,505
<i>Lately, Runch and that new girl</i>

534
00:43:42,585 --> 00:43:44,985
<i>seem awfully close.</i>

535
00:43:45,065 --> 00:43:46,825
Today, you made me feel

536
00:43:46,905 --> 00:43:49,385
like you have a secret life
I don't know about.

537
00:43:49,465 --> 00:43:52,025
You punk! You ruined everything!

538
00:43:52,105 --> 00:43:55,585
You're one to talk. What are you doing?
Finding a side chick for your daughter?

539
00:43:56,985 --> 00:44:00,505
I only did it
because I was trying to protect you.

540
00:44:00,585 --> 00:44:03,825
I won't let anyone
hurt my wife's feelings.

541
00:44:04,865 --> 00:44:07,545
No one. Not even you, Mom.

542
00:44:52,745 --> 00:44:55,105
